WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.800
Yeah, so I think it's actually really hard

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.230
to know where your moderate intensity domain ends.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.810
So where the top of your zone two training

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.740
would be without doing lab testing

5
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:14.290
and measuring lactate.

6
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.660
Zone two can look really different

7
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.450
in different populations.

8
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.550
Elite athletes, I think Tadej Pogačar

9
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.820
was on a podcast,

10
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.520
said his zone two training intensity

11
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.330
can be 320 watts in some rides.

12
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.680
We have recreationally active young adults

13
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.120
whose zone two lactate threshold

14
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.690
would be like 60 watts.

15
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.830
So that's a huge difference.

16
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.350
So any sort of targeting a heart rate

17
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.280
as a percent of max heart rate

18
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.170
is probably not very accurate.

19
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.260
Ventilatory response, maybe you can kind of

20
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.300
use that idea of

21
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.830
if you're talking comfortably,

22
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.770
you might be in zone two.

23
00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.140
But if you're a fit person

24
00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.160
with a really high lactate threshold,

25
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.660
your ventilation is gonna be high

26
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.590
even though you're still in zone two.

27
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.580
So yeah, unfortunately, I think

28
00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.780
if you really wanna know

29
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.690
am I in the moderate intensity domain,

30
00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.680
you have to be either doing

31
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.100
a lot of lab testing

32
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.580
or measuring your lactate,

33
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.930
making sure lactate stays below two millimolar.
